From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:52:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] gdb: do not stop for a condition error when the thread
 is gone

Non-stop: a memory error from a condition in an exiting process gave a bogus breakpoint stop (bug 18749).

diff --git a/gdb/breakpoint.c b/gdb/breakpoint.c
index a23f5998b20..e6f36f3285c 100644
--- a/gdb/breakpoint.c
+++ b/gdb/breakpoint.c
@@ -6053,6 +6053,21 @@ bpstat_check_breakpoint_conditions (bpstat *bs, thread_info *thread)
 	    }
 	  catch (const gdb_exception_error &ex)
 	    {
+	      /* In non-stop mode the other threads run while we evaluate
+		 the condition, and the process may exit meanwhile.  The
+		 error is then no fault of the condition: the exit is
+		 already on its way.  Do not stop and do not complain.  */
+	      if (ex.error == MEMORY_ERROR
+		  && !target_thread_alive (thread->ptid))
+		{
+		  infrun_debug_printf ("thread %s is gone, condition not "
+				       "evaluated: %s",
+				       thread->ptid.to_string ().c_str (),
+				       ex.what ());
+		  bs->stop = false;
+		  return;
+		}
+
 	      int locno = bpstat_locno (bs);
 	      if (locno != 0)
 		exception_fprintf
